# /etc/mtc-bridge/mtc-bridge.env  —  CONTRACT ONLY. NAMES, NEVER VALUES.
#
# Target state: owner root:root, mode 0600, referenced by EnvironmentFile= in
# the bridge unit. install.sh creates this file from this template with every
# variable left UNSET and never writes a value into it.
#
# Filling it in is a separate, owner-only action under KVM2-P4-03 (TESTNET-only
# secret provisioning). Install, deploy and audit authorization do NOT authorize
# it. No value from this file may ever appear in the repository, a chat session,
# a prompt, a task list, shell history, a screenshot or a plaintext backup.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for TESTNET operation (provisioned only under KVM2-P4-03)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   HL_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS   Hyperliquid main account address (0x + 40 hex).
#                        Identifies the account; holds no spending authority.
#   HL_API_WALLET_KEY    Private key of a VPS-SPECIFIC named agent/API wallet
#                        (0x + 64 hex). Never the main wallet key. An agent
#                        wallet cannot withdraw, and revoking it revokes only
#                        this host.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL (feature stays silently disabled when unset)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN   Alert bot token; outbound alert only.
#   TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID     Alert destination chat id.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY    Claude veto layer. LLM can only reduce risk.
#   XAI_API_KEY          Grok regime layer. LLM can only reduce risk.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORBIDDEN — must be ABSENT from this file, from the unit, and from the
# service process environment. Its presence is a hard stop at KVM2-P4-03,
# KVM2-P4-07, KVM2-P4-08B and KVM2-P5-05A.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   HL_LIVE_ACK
#
# Note: MTC_BRIDGE_STATE_DB is set by the unit itself (Environment=), not here,
# so the state path stays part of the hashed unit rather than of the secret file.
